meta {
  name: Delete Referral Panel
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/referral-panels/{{referralPanelId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `branch_admin:referrals__delete_referral_panel` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.
  
  Soft-delete a referral panel (sets `deletedAt`). Cascades a soft-delete to its
  active assigned lab tests and lab panels in the same transaction. Scoped to the
  caller's tenant.

  Uses `referralPanelId` captured by *Create Referral Panel (Percentage
  Commission)*. Run this last — once deleted, *Get* / *Update* against the same id
  return 404 `REFERRAL_PANEL_NOT_FOUND`, and the panel's name / panel code are
  freed for reuse.

  **409 `REFERRAL_PANEL_IN_USE`** — deletion is blocked when the panel is used by an
  order still in an active accessioning/technician-stage workflow (a non-cancelled
  order with a sample still being collected/processed, or a lab report not yet published). Deactivate the panel
  instead (`PATCH` with `isActive: false`). Historical / fully-published / cancelled
  orders do **not** block deletion.
}
